meta {
  name: Backfill Historical Data
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/market-data/:symbol/backfill?days=10
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  days: 10
  ~start_date: 2025-11-01T00:00:00
  ~end_date: 2025-11-30T23:59:59
  ~month: 2024-01
  ~year: 2024
}

params:path {
  symbol: SPY
}

docs {
  Manually trigger backfill of historical data

  Automatically detects and fills any gaps in the data.

  Four ways to specify date range (use only ONE):
  1. Days back (EASIER): Use days parameter (e.g., days=7)
  2. Explicit dates: Use start_date and end_date (uncomment in params)
  3. Single month: Use month parameter (e.g., month=2024-01)
  4. Entire year: Use year parameter (e.g., year=2024)

  Query params (use only ONE):
  - days: Number of days to backfill from today (1-30)
  - start_date + end_date: Explicit date range (ISO format, max 30 days)
  - month: Single month in YYYY-MM format (e.g., 2024-01)
  - year: Entire year (e.g., 2024) - processes all 12 months sequentially

  Returns:
  - symbol
  - start_date / end_date (for days/dates/month)
  - bars_inserted
  - gaps_found
  - gaps[] (array of gap details)
  - success

  Year backfill also returns:
  - year
  - total_bars_inserted
  - total_gaps_found
  - months_processed
  - monthly_results[] (detailed results per month)
  - failed_months[]
}
